        #revision
          %p
            Differential endofunctors and differential monads appear in the treatment of differential calculus on noncommutative spaces/schemes represented by their abelian categories “of quasicoherent sheaves”; the formalism is due
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Valery+Lunts"} Valery Lunts
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"} Alexander Rosenberg
          %h4#filtrations_associated_to_topologizing_subcategories Filtrations associated to topologizing subcategories
          %p
            Below, a “subscheme” of an abelian category is in the sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topologizing+subcategory"} topologizing subcategory
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            be an abelian category
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            satisfying the Gabriel’s
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/property+sup"} property sup
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕋
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            of
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            one defines the notion of
            %strong
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
              \-filtration
            on any object
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            of
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            as an increasing
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mo ⋅
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi i
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_\cdot = \{M_i \,|\, i\gt -1\}
            on
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            such that
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{-1} = 0
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ob
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_i/M_{i-1} \in Ob \mathbb{T}
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕋
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            there is a canonical choice of a
            = succeed "-filtration" do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_i = \mathbb{T}^{(i+1)}M
            (see
            = succeed ");" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-th+neighborhood+of+a+topologizing+subcategory"} n-th neighborhood of a topologizing subcategory
            = succeed "-torsion" do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕋
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^{i+1}
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi sup
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^{(\infty)}(M) := sup\{\mathbb{T}^{(i)}M\}
            which is calle the
            %strong
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
              \-part
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "-object" do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            = succeed "-part." do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^\infty
            (note no brackets in the notation) the full subcategory of
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            whose objects are
            = succeed "-objects." do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
          %p
            %strong Proposition.
            (Lunts-Rosenberg MPI1996-53, Lemma 3.3.1) The subcategory
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝕋
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}^\infty
            is a coreflective topologizing subcategory of
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %h4#the_case_of_the_diagonal_subscheme_differential_filtration The case of the diagonal “subscheme”: differential filtration
          %p
            Fix an abelian category
            = succeed ";" do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %mi End
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = End A
            be the category of additive endofunctors
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to A
            (essential smallness or some sort of accessibility assumption may be required on
            = succeed ")." do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            has the Gabriel’s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/property+sup"} property sup
            then
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi End
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End A
            also has the property sup).
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕋
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            be the diagonal subscheme of
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_34.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo =
                    %mi End
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = End A
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_35.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi End
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End A
            containing the identity functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_36.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_A
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_37.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the category
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_38.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_R Mod
            for
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_39.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a simple ring, then all “subschemes” of it are (Zariski) closed.
          %p
            %strong Definition.
            The
            = succeed "-part" do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_40.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_41.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            of
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_42.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %mi End
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = End A
            is called the
            %strong differential part
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_43.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            = succeed "-objects" do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_44.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_45.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            are called
            = succeed "." do
              %strong differential endofunctors
            %strong differential monad
            is a monad whose underlying endofunctor is differential.
          %p
            In these definitions it is often convenient to redefine
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_46.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            as some other full subcategory
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_47.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi End
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \subset End A
            containing
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_48.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_A
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_49.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi End
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End A
          %h4#the_case_of_noncommutative_rings The case of (noncommutative) rings
          %p
            If
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_50.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is the category
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_51.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}_R Mod
            and
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_52.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi End
                    %mi c
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = End_c A
            of endofunctors having right adjoint for a (possibly noncommutative associative)
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_53.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_54.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+bimodule"} differential bimodule
            = succeed "-part" do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_55.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_R
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_56.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_R
            is (basically, by the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Watts+theorem"} Eilenberg-Watts theorem
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_57.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\otimes_k R^{op}
            = succeed "-bimodules)" do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_58.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_59.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_60.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi k
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\otimes_k R^{op}
            contained in
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_bc1bc968e6a145c58a8be909ec4f8722611212cb_61.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ann
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ann(m)
          %h3#literature Literature
          %p The general abstract nonsense is proposed in these 1996 MPI preprints:
          %ul
            %li
              V. A. Lunts,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"} A. L. Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential calculus in noncommutative algebraic geometry I. D-calculus on noncommutative rings
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preblob/3894"} pdf
              = succeed "," do
                %em II. D-Calculus in the braided case. The localization of quantized enveloping algebras
              %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preblob/3916"} pdf
          %p This is applied (without mentioning differential monads) to the case of noncommutative rings in
          %ul
            %li
              V. A. Lunts,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"} A. L. Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential operators on noncommutative rings
              %strong 3
              (1997), no. 3, 335–359 (
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s000290050014"}> doi
              ); sequel:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Localization for quantum groups
              %strong 5
              (1999), no. 1, pp. 123–159 (
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s000290050044"}> doi
              ).
